// PARAM: --analysis interval --solver warrow --context call-string --context-depth 1
// n is concretely 1 or 2, so n < 10 holds -- but Apinis warrowing under a
// depth-1 call string cannot establish it. Mechanism: depth 1 keeps only the
// innermost call site, so both activations of q enter p at the single
// context [q:p(m)], and that one FunctionEntry seed is written by two
// origins. The first write leaves it at [1,1]; the second recomputes the
// join as [1,2] and widens [1,1] against it, and since the upper bound grew
// it goes to +inf. Neither producer's own contribution ever moved -- the
// growth is an artifact of widening a value already joined across origins,
// the same loss as 03-warrow_joins_before_widening.vimp, now reached
// through the context lifter's collapse rather than two direct call sites.
//
// 15-solver-choice/precision/07-warrow_per_origin_call_string.vimp is the
// same program under --solver warrow-per-origin and answers PROVED.
void p(int32 n) {
  __voblint_check(n < 10) // UNKNOWN
}
void q(int32 m) {
  p(m)
}
void main() {
  q(1);
  q(2)
}
